 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch 24 not draining, water sitting in bottom. help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can help with that. To make sure I give you the correct safety steps and location of the parts, is this a washing machine or a tumble dryer? The '24' likely refers to the 60cm width, but Bosch uses similar numbering for both types."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "dishwasher. freestanding Bosch, model SMS24AW01G. display shows E:24"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "The E:24 code on your Bosch SMS24AW01G confirms a drainage fault – the machine has detected that water isn't leaving. This is most commonly caused by a blocked filter or debris stuck in the pump impeller. Please switch off and unplug the dishwasher first. Remove the bottom rack, then twist and lift out the main filter assembly at the base of the tub. Check if it is blocked with food or grease, and look into the sump (the hole underneath) for any foreign objects like glass shards, bones, or bottle caps that might be jamming the impeller. Did you find anything blocking the filter or caught in the pump area?\n[Helpful to see: image \"Where the filter is\" — The filter sits in the base of the dishwasher, usually under the bottom spray arm. Twist it out anticlockwise and rinse it under a tap. Typical layout — your dishwasher may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "filter clogged with food and some broken glass. wore gloves? no, will do. cleaned it"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Blocked filter and pump impeller]\nGood work clearing that out – glass and food debris are very common causes of E:24 on Bosch dishwashers. Then run a short drain or rinse cycle to see if it pumps the water out correctly now."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ran it. drains normally now, E:24 gone"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Blocked filter and pump impeller (glass/food)]\nThat is excellent news. The E:24 code was caused by the glass and food debris blocking the drain pump impeller, which has now been cleared. To prevent this happening again, try to scrape large bits of food off dishes before loading, and avoid putting small items like bottle caps or olive stones in the machine where they can wash down into the sump."
  }
 ],
